{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "760e171f-6d75-46e8-a538-18599eecb720",
    "name": "Genome Properties REST API",
    "description": "Smoke tests for the Genome Properties REST API.\n\nLocal Django (uv run python manage.py runserver):\n- baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:8000\n- apiRoot = api/v1\n- healthPath = health/\n\nDev ingress (https://wwwdev.ebi.ac.uk):\n- baseUrl = https://wwwdev.ebi.ac.uk\n- apiRoot = interpro/genomeproperties/api/v1\n- healthPath = interpro/genomeproperties/api/health/\n\nAssignment success calls need DATABASE_PATH pointing at genome_properties.db. Empty and unknown-format assignment calls do not.\nThe multipart file request resolves postman/fixtures/interpro-entries.tsv from the repository root.\nSwagger UI: {{baseUrl}}/{{apiRoot}}/docs",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "_exporter_id": "19420352"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Docs",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "OpenAPI schema",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"HTTP 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test(\"JSON content type\", () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get(\"Content-Type\")).to.match(/application\\/json/);",
                  "});",
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "const paths = Object.keys(json.paths);",
                  "pm.test(\"OpenAPI 3\", () => pm.expect(json.openapi).to.match(/^3\\./));",
                  "pm.test(\"Title\", () => pm.expect(json.info.title).to.eql(\"Genome Properties API\"));",
                  "pm.test(\"Version\", () => pm.expect(json.info.version).to.eql(\"1.0.0\"));",
                  "pm.test(\"Versioned paths\", () => pm.expect(paths.every((path) => path.includes(\"/v1/\"))).to.eql(true));",
                  "function hasPathEnding(suffix) {",
                  "    return paths.some((path) => path.endsWith(suffix));",
                  "}",
                  "pm.test(\"Has health path\", () => pm.expect(hasPathEnding(\"/health\")).to.eql(true));",
                  "pm.test(\"Has genome-properties path\", () => pm.expect(hasPathEnding(\"/genome-properties\")).to.eql(true));",
                  "pm.test(\"Has property detail path\", () => pm.expect(hasPathEnding(\"/genome-properties/{accession}\")).to.eql(true));",
                  "pm.test(\"Has hierarchy path\", () => pm.expect(hasPathEnding(\"/hierarchy/{accession}\")).to.eql(true));",
                  "pm.test(\"Has assign path\", () => pm.expect(hasPathEnding(\"/assign\")).to.eql(true));",
                  "pm.test(\"Assign is POST\", () => {",
                  "    const assignPath = paths.find((path) => path.endsWith(\"/assign\"));",
                  "    pm.expect(json.paths[assignPath]).to.have.property(\"post\");",
                  "    pm.expect(json.paths[assignPath]).to.not.have.property(\"get\");",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test(\"Property list is GET\", () => {",
                  "    const listPath = paths.find((path) => path.endsWith(\"/genome-properties\"));",
                  "    pm.expect(json.paths[listPath]).to.have.property(\"get\");",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/{{apiRoot}}/openapi.json",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "{{apiRoot}}",
                "openapi.json"
              ]
            },
            "description": "OpenAPI 3 document for the versioned API."
          },
          "response": []
        },
